A||||1||montage||Front 88 offset 37mm???||||1||
Z||000000||montage||06-10-2001||07:30 AM||||On the inside of my 88 formula wheels is stamped: 15X6 37 mm. Is this the proper offset for 88 fronts? I've done several searches and most here on the forum state it is 45 mm. I'm in the process of new tires and wheels so correct information would be helpful. Maybe those that have a service manual could find the value in there. I would appreciate any comments. I guess the next step for me is to measure the offset when I do a brake job this week. I'll keep you posted.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||06-10-2001||09:34 AM||||I believe that is correct. If they are factory rims, an easy way to check is look for a 'lip' on the face of rim. If no lip, '88 rims. The ones for the rear have a 'lip', so if you have one pair that doesn't match the other pair in this area then you have proper rims.<BR>Hope this makes sense to you!<BR>Or you can search the archives on the subject!||||reg||1
